meta {
  name: getclassresults
  type: http
  seq: 4
}

get {
  url: {{legacyBase}}/api.php?method=getclassresults&comp={{compId}}&class={{className}}&unformattedTimes=true
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  method: getclassresults
  comp: {{compId}}
  class: {{className}}
  unformattedTimes: true
  ~last_hash: paste-a-hash-here
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  Pairs with new-api/Class results. The important side-by-side.

  Sent with `unformattedTimes=true`, as the server does today. **Disable that
  parameter** to see the formatted variant (`"19:03"`, `"+02:51"`) — the new API has
  no such switch and is always integers.

  Look for:

  - `splitcontrols` (lowercase c) → `splitControls`
  - `hash` + `status` → `ETag` header
  - `DT_RowClass: "new_result"` → `changed` / `startChanged` UNIX seconds
  - no `bib`, no `isMultiDay` / `isMassStart` / `qualificationLimits`
  - split maps have no `_changed` key

  `DT_RowClass` is the one the plan has to synthesise: the client compares each row's
  `changed` against a stored high-water mark and re-adds the flag, so
  `live-class-writer.ts` and the app's "new result" highlight keep working unchanged.
}
